Package: fragcorr
Type: Package
Title: Fragment-Level Spatial Correlation of CpG Methylation
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Yucheng", "Wang", email = "ychwang0331@gmail.com",
                  role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Estimates how strongly the methylation states of CpGs on the same
    sequenced DNA fragment co-vary, as a function of the distance between them,
    from bisulfite sequencing reads in the wgbstools .pat / .beta formats. Each
    region and cell type receives a posterior distribution over an exponential
    correlation kernel rho(d) = phi * exp(-d / s), defined on the latent probit
    scale and conditional on each CpG's own methylation rate. Fragment
    likelihoods are multivariate normal orthant probabilities, computed by
    expectation propagation; a prior over kernels is fitted per methylation bin
    by empirical Bayes.
License: file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 4.1)
Imports: data.table, mixsqp, Rcpp, parallel, stats, utils
LinkingTo: Rcpp, RcppArmadillo
Suggests: testthat (>= 3.0.0), mvtnorm
